{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Gather.</b> Assemble, and like it is לכנוס את הגרים." "<b>Who are in Shushan.</b> The city." "<b>Fast for me.</b> On my behalf." "<b>Three days.</b> Until the third day, and behold they did not eat in the evening and they fasted two days and two nights, for the verse is night and day, and behold Esther trusted in the Elohim of YHWH; therefore she fasted and did not trust in her beauty, for the face of one who fasts changes, even on the third day." "<b>And when I am lost.</b> That I no longer dwell with my people, utterly lost, and a past-tense verb comes in place of future, and the meaning is according to her thought, and like it: וכאשר שכלתי שכלתי."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:02.126306241Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}